        </a>
    </section>

    <section class="bp-admin-help-overview" aria-label="Admin workflow map">
        <nav class="bp-card bp-admin-help-quicknav" aria-label="Admin help sections">
            <span class="bp-summary-title">Page map</span>
            <strong>Find the exact admin task</strong>
            <a href="#target-state">Target state</a>
            <a href="#workflow-steps">Workflow steps</a>
            <a href="#status-dictionary">Status dictionary</a>
            <a href="#ready-checklist">Ready checklist</a>
        </nav>

        <div class="bp-admin-help-lifecycle" aria-label="Battery passport lifecycle">
            <article>
                <span>01</span>
                <strong>Draft</strong>
                <small>Create the DID and save incomplete admin data safely.</small>
            </article>
            <article>
                <span>02</span>
                <strong>Validate</strong>
                <small>Run schema, business-rule, and completion-policy checks.</small>
            </article>
            <article>
                <span>03</span>
                <strong>Sign</strong>
                <small>Hash and sign the canonical passport core.</small>
            </article>
            <article>
                <span>04</span>
                <strong>Publish</strong>
                <small>Expose only a clean passport with a current proof.</small>
            </article>
            <article>
                <span>05</span>
                <strong>Recover</strong>
                <small>After edits, validate and sign again to leave dirty state.</small>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="target-state" class="bp-admin-help-grid">
        <article class="bp-card bp-admin-help-callout">
            <span class="bp-summary-title">The target state</span>
            <h2>How the battery needs to be</h2>
            <p>
                A battery passport is considered ready when it has been validated, signed, and published with the
                current passport core still clean.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Validated:</strong> the latest validation has zero blocking validation errors.</li>
                <li><strong>Signed:</strong> the current canonical passport core has a signature proof.</li>
                <li><strong>Clean:</strong> the current data still matches the latest signed hash.</li>
                <li><strong>Published:</strong> the registry status is public and publish uses a current valid signature proof.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="bp-card bp-admin-help-callout is-warning">
            <span class="bp-summary-title">Dirty state rule</span>
            <h2>What makes trust dirty?</h2>
            <p>
                Editing saved passport core data after signing makes the passport dirty because the signed hash no longer
                represents the current content.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                HTTP telemetry does not make the passport dirty because live operational requests are outside the signed
                canonical passport core.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="bp-card bp-admin-help-callout">
            <span class="bp-summary-title">Public discovery</span>
            <h2>What users can find</h2>
            <p>
                Public search, registry discovery, and direct public passport URLs expose only passports that are
                published, signed, clean, and verifiable.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Draft, dirty, unsigned, or unpublished passports stay visible to admins so they can be completed,
                validated, signed, and published from the admin workflow.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="bp-card bp-admin-help-callout bp-admin-help-policy-link">
            <span class="bp-summary-title">Completion policy</span>
            <h2>Who decides required data?</h2>
            <p>
                The <strong>Data requirements tab</strong> controls which parameters are required for completion and
                which are optional. Admin required/optional switches are saved in MongoDB in the
                <code>dataCompletionPolicies</code> collection.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Validation, signing, publishing, and conformance checklists read that saved policy before deciding if a
                battery is complete.
            </p>
            <a href="/admin/clusters?tab=data-requirements" class="bp-secondary-button bp-button-compact mt-3">Open data requirements</a>
        </article>
    </section>

    <section id="workflow-steps" class="bp-card">
        <div class="bp-admin-help-section-heading">
            <span class="bp-summary-title">Main workflow</span>
            <h2>Step by step</h2>
            <p>Follow these steps in order when creating a new passport or when repairing an edited passport.</p>
        </div>

        <ol class="bp-admin-help-steps">
            <li class="bp-admin-help-step-card">
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-number">1</div>
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-copy">
                    <h3>Create battery ID</h3>
                    <p>
                        Go to <strong>Administration -> New passport</strong>. The app proposes a Battery Pass DID such as
                        <code>did:web:acme.battery.pass:&lt;unique-id&gt;</code>. Keep that format unless you have a
                        project-specific DID naming rule.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Fill the visible identity fields first: passport ID, name, model number, serial number,
                        manufacturer, manufacturing date, battery mass, category, and registry status.
                    </p>
                    <p class="mb-0">
                        Save the draft. Save draft is always allowed for admins, even if required data is still missing.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="bp-admin-help-step-card">
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-number">2</div>
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-copy">
                    <h3>Fill battery information</h3>
                    <p>
                        Work through the admin form sections and complete the battery facts before trying to sign. The
                        conformance page will show the exact field paths that still need attention.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        If your team wants a field to stop blocking completion, open the <strong>Data requirements tab</strong>
                        and change its required/optional switch. The next validation run will follow the MongoDB-saved
                        policy.
                    </p>
                    <div class="bp-admin-help-required-grid">
                        <div>
                            <h4>Required data</h4>
                            <ul>
                                <li>General product identity and manufacturer details.</li>
                                <li>Battery category, mass, status, manufacturing date, and facility/location details.</li>
                                <li>Material composition and recycled-content values.</li>
                                <li>Performance and durability values such as capacity, energy, voltage, and lifetime metrics.</li>
                                <li>Carbon footprint values, lifecycle stages, and study reference data.</li>
                                <li>Labels, certificates, declarations, circularity, and due-diligence report references where the schema requires them.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <h4>Optional data</h4>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Battery image choice and descriptive display text.</li>
                                <li>Cluster assignment, unless your access-control scenario requires it.</li>
                                <li>Supporting documents that are not required by the schema for signing.</li>
                                <li>Live telemetry and operational HTTP request data.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bp-admin-help-parameter-guide">
                        <div class="bp-admin-help-mini-heading">
                            <span class="bp-summary-title">Parameter-by-parameter fill list</span>
                            <h4>Fill these fields before validation and signing</h4>
                            <p>
                                Use this as the practical admin checklist. The label is what you see in the form; the
                                path shows where the value lands in the passport data.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="bp-admin-help-parameter-grid">
                            <article>
                                <h5>General</h5>
                                <ul class="bp-admin-help-parameter-list">
                                    <li><strong>Passport ID</strong><span><code>passportId</code>. Keep the DID unique and stable.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Name</strong><span><code>app.display.name</code>. Human-readable battery name.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Model Number</strong><span><code>app.display.modelNumber</code> and <code>productIdentifier</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Serial Number</strong><span><code>app.display.serialNumber</code> and manufacturer identifier fallback.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Category</strong><span><code>aspects.generalProductInformation.payload.batteryCategory</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Status</strong><span><code>aspects.generalProductInformation.payload.batteryStatus</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Battery mass</strong><span><code>aspects.generalProductInformation.payload.batteryMass</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Manufactured date</strong><span><code>aspects.generalProductInformation.payload.manufacturingDate</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Facility ID</strong><span><code>app.display.facilityId</code>. Fill when the facility/location is known.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Manufactured by</strong><span><code>app.display.manufacturerName</code> and manufacturer contact name.</span></li>
                                </ul>
                            </article>

                            <article>
                                <h5>Material composition</h5>
                                <ul class="bp-admin-help-parameter-list">
                                    <li><strong>Nickel kg</strong><span><code>batteryMaterials[].batteryMaterialMass</code> for Nickel.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Copper kg</strong><span><code>batteryMaterials[].batteryMaterialMass</code> for Copper.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Aluminium kg</strong><span><code>batteryMaterials[].batteryMaterialMass</code> for Aluminium.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Graphite kg</strong><span><code>batteryMaterials[].batteryMaterialMass</code> for Graphite.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Manganese kg</strong><span><code>batteryMaterials[].batteryMaterialMass</code> for Manganese.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Cobalt kg</strong><span><code>batteryMaterials[].batteryMaterialMass</code> for Cobalt.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Lithium kg</strong><span><code>batteryMaterials[].batteryMaterialMass</code> for Lithium.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Electrolyte and separators kg</strong><span><code>batteryMaterials[].batteryMaterialMass</code> for electrolyte/separator material.</span></li>
                                </ul>
                            </article>

                            <article>
                                <h5>Performance</h5>
                                <ul class="bp-admin-help-parameter-list">
                                    <li><strong>Rated energy kWh</strong><span><code>batteryTechicalProperties.ratedEnergy</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Rated capacity Ah</strong><span><code>batteryTechicalProperties.ratedCapacity</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Maximum power kW</strong><span><code>batteryTechicalProperties.ratedMaximumPower</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Nominal voltage V</strong><span><code>batteryTechicalProperties.nominalVoltage</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Expected lifetime years</strong><span><code>batteryTechicalProperties.expectedLifetime</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Expected cycles</strong><span><code>batteryTechicalProperties.expectedNumberOfCycles</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>State of charge %</strong><span><code>batteryCondition.stateOfCharge.stateOfChargeValue</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Remaining capacity %</strong><span><code>batteryCondition.remainingCapacity.remainingCapacityValue</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Remaining energy kWh</strong><span><code>batteryCondition.remainingEnergy.remainingEnergyValue</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Full cycles</strong><span><code>batteryCondition.numberOfFullCycles.numberOfFullCyclesValue</code>.</span></li>
                                </ul>
                            </article>

                            <article>
                                <h5>Compliance</h5>
                                <ul class="bp-admin-help-parameter-list">
                                    <li><strong>Conformity assessment report</strong><span><code>aspects.labeling.payload.resultOfTestReport</code>. Add a URL or document reference.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>EU declaration of conformity</strong><span><code>aspects.labeling.payload.declarationOfConformity</code>. Add a URL or document reference.</span></li>
                                </ul>
                            </article>

                            <article>
                                <h5>Supply chain</h5>
                                <ul class="bp-admin-help-parameter-list">
                                    <li><strong>Supply chain index</strong><span><code>aspects.supplyChainDueDiligence.payload.supplyChainIndicies</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Sustainability report</strong><span><code>aspects.supplyChainDueDiligence.payload.sustainabilityReport</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Due diligence report</strong><span><code>aspects.supplyChainDueDiligence.payload.supplyChainDueDiligenceReport</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Third-party audit</strong><span><code>aspects.supplyChainDueDiligence.payload.thirdPartyAussurances</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Taxonomy report</strong><span><code>aspects.supplyChainDueDiligence.payload.taxonomyReport</code>.</span></li>
                                </ul>
                            </article>

                            <article>
                                <h5>Circularity</h5>
                                <ul class="bp-admin-help-parameter-list">
                                    <li><strong>Separate collection</strong><span><code>endOfLifeInformation.separateCollection</code>. Add collection instructions or URL.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Waste prevention</strong><span><code>endOfLifeInformation.wastePrevention</code>. Add prevention instructions or URL.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Recycled content share verification</strong><span><code>app.notes.circularity.recycledContentShareVerification</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Nickel pre/post/primary %</strong><span><code>recycledContent</code> row for Nickel.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Cobalt pre/post/primary %</strong><span><code>recycledContent</code> row for Cobalt.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Lithium pre/post/primary %</strong><span><code>recycledContent</code> row for Lithium.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Lead pre/post/primary %</strong><span><code>recycledContent</code> row for Lead.</span></li>
                                </ul>
                            </article>

                            <article>
                                <h5>Carbon Footprint</h5>
                                <ul class="bp-admin-help-parameter-list">
                                    <li><strong>Amount gCO2e/kWh</strong><span><code>aspects.carbonFootprintForBatteries.payload.batteryCarbonFootprint</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Performance class</strong><span><code>carbonFootprintPerformanceClass</code>.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Raw material extraction gCO2e/kWh</strong><span><code>carbonFootprintPerLifecycleStage</code> for raw material extraction.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Main production gCO2e/kWh</strong><span><code>carbonFootprintPerLifecycleStage</code> for main production.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Distribution gCO2e/kWh</strong><span><code>carbonFootprintPerLifecycleStage</code> for distribution.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>Recycling gCO2e/kWh</strong><span><code>carbonFootprintPerLifecycleStage</code> for recycling.</span></li>
                                    <li><strong>CO2 study reference</strong><span><code>aspects.carbonFootprintForBatteries.payload.carbonFootprintStudy</code>. Add a URL or document reference.</span></li>
                                </ul>
                            </article>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="mb-0">
                        If a generated schema field is not exposed by the friendly form, use the conformance page
                        completion checklist to identify the missing field. For demonstrator setup, the
                        <strong>Complete required demo data</strong> action appears only while required data is still
                        incomplete. When the data is already complete, that action is hidden.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="bp-admin-help-step-card">
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-number">3</div>
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-copy">
                    <h3>Validate passport</h3>
                    <p>
                        Open the passport conformance page and click <strong>Validate passport</strong>. Validation checks
                        the official Battery Pass schemas and the practical business rules that the schemas do not fully
                        express.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        If blocking errors remain, the page lists the section, data point path, and correction guidance.
                        Fix those fields and validate again.
                    </p>
                    <p class="mb-0">
                        The <strong>Sign passport</strong> action appears only after validation reports zero blocking
                        validation errors.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="bp-admin-help-step-card">
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-number">4</div>
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-copy">
                    <h3>Sign passport</h3>
                    <p>
                        When the conformance page says <strong>Can sign: Yes</strong>, click <strong>Sign passport</strong>.
                        The app canonicalizes the passport core, creates a hash, stores proof metadata, and records an
                        immutable signed revision.
                    </p>
                    <p class="mb-0">
                        After signing, the trust state should become clean because the current passport data matches the
                        latest signed revision.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="bp-admin-help-step-card">
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-number">5</div>
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-copy">
                    <h3>Publish passport</h3>
                    <p>
                        Publishing requires a current valid signature proof. The <strong>Publish passport</strong> action
                        appears only after the current passport core has been signed and verifies cleanly.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Once published, the public passport summary is available. Privileged trust/conformance evidence
                        lives in the detailed report under the <strong>Trust &amp; conformance</strong> tab for authorized admins only.
                    </p>
                    <p class="mb-0">
                        The <strong>Trust &amp; conformance tab is visible only</strong> to general admins or local cluster admins for the battery's cluster.
                        Normal cluster users can open the detail report, but they do not see the privileged trust evidence tab.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="bp-admin-help-step-card">
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-number">6</div>
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-copy">
                    <h3>Edit after publishing</h3>
                    <p>
                        Admins can still edit a published or signed passport. After saving a core-data edit, the passport
                        becomes dirty because the old signature was made over the previous canonical content.
                    </p>
                    <p class="mb-0">
                        Do not treat the old signature as current after an edit. Use the dirty-to-clean workflow below.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="bp-admin-help-step-card">
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-number">7</div>
                <div class="bp-admin-help-step-copy">
                    <h3>Move from dirty back to clean</h3>
                    <p>
                        Open conformance, validate the updated data, fix every blocking error, sign again, and publish the
                        latest signed revision.
                    </p>
                    <p class="mb-0">
                        The passport is clean again only when the current core data verifies against the newest signature
                        proof and the publish gate is no longer blocked.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="status-dictionary" class="bp-card">
        <div class="bp-admin-help-section-heading">
            <span class="bp-summary-title">Status dictionary</span>
            <h2>What each state means</h2>
            <p>Use these terms when deciding whether a battery is ready for a customer or regulator to inspect.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bp-admin-help-state-grid">
            <article>
                <h3>Draft</h3>
                <p>Editable admin data. Draft can be incomplete and unsigned, but it should not be treated as trusted.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
                <h3>Validated</h3>
                <p>The latest validation completed with zero blockers. Validation alone is not a signature.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
                <h3>Signed</h3>
                <p>The canonical passport core has a hash and proof metadata stored in a signed revision.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
                <h3>Clean</h3>
                <p>The current passport core still matches the latest signed hash.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
                <h3>Dirty</h3>
                <p>The passport core changed after signing. Validate and sign again before relying on it.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
                <h3>Published</h3>
                <p>The passport is public and should have a current valid signature proof before being shown as trusted.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="ready-checklist" class="bp-card bp-admin-help-checklist">
        <div>
            <span class="bp-summary-title">Quick checklist</span>
            <h2>Before you say this battery is ready</h2>
        </div>
        <ul>
            <li>The admin form has all visible required identity, manufacturer, material, performance, carbon, circularity, label, and due-diligence data filled.</li>
            <li>The conformance page shows zero blocking validation errors.</li>
            <li>The passport has been signed after the latest data change.</li>
            <li>The trust state is Clean, not Dirty.</li>
            <li>The publish gate says publishing is allowed.</li>
            <li>The detailed report shows proof information in the Trust &amp; conformance tab for general admins or local cluster admins for the battery's cluster.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</main>
